{UTF-8}
{ Chapter 28: trucks at a fuel depot with 4 loading bays, each loading a truck in 30 minutes on average. Arrivals rise for a morning peak. Two aggregate formulations run side by side: a plain fluid model and a fluid model whose loading rate comes from queueing theory (generated by scripts/ch28_build.py). }
Base Arrivals=
	5
	~	truck/hour
	~	Trucks arriving per hour outside the peak.
	|
Peak Extra=
	2.6
	~	truck/hour
	~	Extra trucks per hour between Peak Start and Peak End.
	|
Peak Start=
	6
	~	hour
	~	|
Peak End=
	10
	~	hour
	~	|
Arrival Rate=
	Base Arrivals + STEP(Peak Extra, Peak Start) - STEP(Peak Extra, Peak End)
	~	truck/hour
	~	Trucks arriving per hour; both models receive the same arrivals.
	|
Fluid Arrivals=
	Arrival Rate
	~	truck/hour
	~	|
Lookup Arrivals=
	Arrival Rate
	~	truck/hour
	~	|
Bays=
	4
	~	truck
	~	Loading bays: trucks that can load at the same time.
	|
Loading Time=
	0.5
	~	hour
	~	Average time to load one truck in a bay (30 minutes).
	|
Loading Capacity=
	Bays / Loading Time
	~	truck/hour
	~	Trucks the depot can load per hour with every bay busy.
	|
Fluid Trucks= INTEG(
	Fluid Arrivals - Fluid Departures,
	0)
	~	truck
	~	Trucks at the depot (waiting or loading), plain fluid model.
	|
Fluid Departures=
	MIN(Fluid Trucks, Bays) / Loading Time
	~	truck/hour
	~	A truck in a bay leaves after the loading time; no truck waits while a bay is free.
	|
Busy Fraction Table(
	[(0,0)-(50.1942,1)],(0.0,0.0),(0.05,0.05),(0.1,0.1),(0.1502,0.15),(0.2006,0.2),(0.2517,0.25),(0.304,0.3),(0.3581,0.35),(0.4151,0.4),(0.4763,0.45),(0.5435,0.5),(0.6193,0.55),(0.7077,0.6),(0.8145,0.65),(0.95,0.7),(1.1321,0.75),(1.3964,0.8),(1.8265,0.85),(2.6724,0.9),(5.1842,0.95),(6.4365,0.96),(8.5221,0.97),(12.691,0.98),(16.8587,0.985),(25.1931,0.99),(50.1942,0.995))
	~	dmnl
	~	Steady-state utilisation of an M/M/4 depot against the mean number of trucks at it per bay (Erlang C), inverted.
	|
Lookup Trucks= INTEG(
	Lookup Arrivals - Lookup Departures,
	0)
	~	truck
	~	Trucks at the depot, fluid model with the queueing lookup.
	|
Busy Fraction=
	Busy Fraction Table(Lookup Trucks / Bays)
	~	dmnl
	~	Share of bay capacity in use, read from the queueing lookup.
	|
Lookup Departures=
	Loading Capacity * Busy Fraction
	~	truck/hour
	~	|
********************************************************
	.Control
********************************************************~
		Simulation Control Parameters
	|
FINAL TIME  = 24
	~	hour
	~	|
INITIAL TIME  = 0
	~	hour
	~	|
SAVEPER  = TIME STEP
	~	hour
	~	|
TIME STEP  = 0.015625
	~	hour
	~	|
